WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.650
A royal hall in northern England.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.200
It is Easter Sunday, and
the king is feasting.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.790
In the same household, the
queen is still fasting.

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.960
For her, it is only Palm Sunday.

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.220
One household.

6
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.140
Two different Easters.

7
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.840
Why did a king and queen keep
Easter on different days?

8
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.920
In this mission, you'll trace an argument
over Easter that began in the second

9
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.960
century and reached the Irish monasteries.

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.720
Then you'll sit in on a
meeting at Whitby in 664,

11
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.930
where the king had to choose
between two traditions.

12
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.950
Your mission: find out
why the dates differed,

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.240
and how the meeting at Whitby settled it.
